From: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Subject: [DEBUG] net: airoha: npu: set streaming DMA mask to avoid swiotlb

The driver only calls dma_set_coherent_mask() but never dma_set_mask().
On this non-coherent ARM64 platform (EN7581), that forces every
dma_map_single() through swiotlb bounce buffers. Debug tracing shows the
NPU firmware permanently hangs after ~41 bounce-buffered mailbox calls.

Replace dma_set_coherent_mask() with dma_set_mask_and_coherent() so
streaming DMA maps directly without swiotlb bounce, matching the
coherent path behavior.

NOT FOR MERGE — debug verification step.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>

---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -769,7 +769,7 @@ static int airoha_npu_probe(struct platf
 		npu->irqs[i] = irq;
 	}

-	err = dma_set_coherent_mask(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	err = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
 	if (err)
 		return err;

